checks_run.procedure:
Step 2. Attack the run-time layer mechanically (R1–R8):
- is the flag in every fork;
- can a file escape it through its environment, the CLI pool, a per-project pool, or the preload;
- does `pnpm test` fail when the canary fails;
- can the project be filtered or wildcarded away;
- is it refused when combined with another project;
- does the flag stay out of the other projects.

Separation of duties and no on-behalf decision in every P3 business approval. Probe B (unchanged) covers:
- B1: the database CHECKs, by INSERT and UPDATE as mth_app;
- B4: a dual-role proposer, and onBehalfOfUserId on the weight-set approval, the Finance validations and override revoke;
- B5: audit shape.
The suites cover the rest.

